From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerry Zhao <jerryz123@berkeley.edu>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 23:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Isolate Sv LR/SC exception signatures

The ExceptionsSvZalrsc tests exercise address translation, exception
selection, and delegation for LR and SC. They execute SYSTEM instructions
between each LR and SC, so the sequence is unconstrained and the SC result is
permitted to indicate failure even when the address is valid.

Keep the existing signature slots but write zero instead of the LR and SC
destinations. A permitted failed SC also leaves memory unchanged, so later LR
values otherwise inherit the same nonarchitectural assumption. The trap
signature continues to check whether each operation raises the required load
or store/AMO exception.

---
 .../sv32_exceptions_Zalrsc_Mmode.S             | 5 +++--
 .../sv32_exceptions_Zalrsc_Smode.S             | 5 +++--
 .../sv32_exceptions_Zalrsc_Umode.S             | 5 +++--
 .../sv39_exceptions_Zalrsc_Mmode.S             | 5 +++--
 .../sv39_exceptions_Zalrsc_Smode.S             | 5 +++--
 .../sv39_exceptions_Zalrsc_Umode.S             | 5 +++--
 6 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/priv/ExceptionsSvZalrsc/sv32_exceptions_Zalrsc_Mmode.S b/tests/priv/ExceptionsSvZalrsc/sv32_exceptions_Zalrsc_Mmode.S
--- a/tests/priv/ExceptionsSvZalrsc/sv32_exceptions_Zalrsc_Mmode.S
+++ b/tests/priv/ExceptionsSvZalrsc/sv32_exceptions_Zalrsc_Mmode.S
@@ -93,7 +93,8 @@ RVTEST_BEGIN
 
   // Signature Update
-  RVTEST_SIGUPD(x2, x5, x4, a3, \TEST_CASE\()_lr, \TEST_CASE\()_lr_str)
-  RVTEST_SIGUPD(x2, x5, x4, a4, \TEST_CASE\()_sc, \TEST_CASE\()_sc_str)
+  // These signatures check exceptions, not results affected by unconstrained SC success.
+  RVTEST_SIGUPD(x2, x5, x4, x0, \TEST_CASE\()_lr, \TEST_CASE\()_lr_str)
+  RVTEST_SIGUPD(x2, x5, x4, x0, \TEST_CASE\()_sc, \TEST_CASE\()_sc_str)
 .endm
 
 .macro SET_REQ_MSTATUS_VAL
